ef1fea9fffac9ad5b01ad0cad4ecb17beef916d8d7503409c553ae91d592"},"seconds":21.87158465385437,"seed":1101158061113523707,"stop":"eos","text":"To find the smallest positive rational number \\( r \\) such that\n\\[\n\\sum_{k=1}^{35} \\sin (5k)^\\circ = \\tan r^\\circ,\n\\]\nwe start by using the sum of sines formula. The sum of sines can be expressed using the formula for the sum of a geometric series. First, we use the identity for the sum of sines:\n\\[\n\\sum_{k=1}^{n} \\sin (kx) = \\frac{\\sin \\left( \\frac{nx}{2} \\right) \\sin \\left( \\frac{(n+1)x}{2} \\right)}{\\sin \\left( \\frac{x}{2} \\right)}.\n\\]\nIn our case, \\( x = 5^\\circ \\) and \\( n = 35 \\), so we have:\n\\[\n\\sum_{k=1}^{35} \\sin (5k)^\\circ = \\frac{\\sin \\left( \\frac{35 \\cdot 5^\\circ}{2} \\right) \\sin \\left( \\frac{36 \\cdot 5^\\circ}{2} \\right)}{\\sin \\left( \\frac{5^\\circ}{2} \\right)} = \\frac{\\sin (87.5^\\circ) \\sin (90^\\circ)}{\\sin (2.5^\\circ)}.\n\\]\nSince \\( \\sin (90^\\circ) = 1 \\), this simplifies to:\n\\[\n\\sum_{k=1}^{35} \\sin (5k)^\\circ = \\frac{\\sin (87.5^\\circ)}{\\sin (2.5^\\circ)}.\n\\]\nUsing the co-function identity \\( \\sin (87.5^\\circ) = \\cos (2.5^\\circ) \\), we get:\n\\[\n\\sum_{k=1}^{35} \\sin (5k)^\\circ = \\frac{\\cos (2.5^\\circ)}{\\sin (2.5^\\circ)} = \\cot (2.5^\\circ) = \\tan (90^\\circ - 2.5^\\circ) = \\tan (87.5^\\circ).\n\\]\nThus, we have:\n\\[\n\\sum_{k=1}^{35} \\sin (5k)^\\circ = \\tan (87.5^\\circ).\n\\]\nSince \\( 87.5^\\circ \\) is not a rational number, we need to find the smallest positive rational number \\( r \\) such that \\( \\tan r^\\circ = \\tan (87.5^\\circ) \\). The tangent function is periodic with period \\( 180^\\circ \\), so we can write:\n\\[\n87.5^\\circ = 180^\\circ - 92.5^\\circ,\n\\]\nand thus:\n\\[\n\\tan (87.5^\\circ) = \\tan (180^\\circ - 92.5^\\circ) = -\\tan (92.5^\\circ).\n\\]\nSince \\( \\tan (92.5^\\circ) = \\cot (2.5^\\circ) \\), we have:\n\\[\n\\tan (87.5^\\circ) = \\tan (90^\\circ - 2.5^\\circ) = \\tan (92.5^\\circ - 180^\\circ) = \\tan (87.5^\\circ).\n\\]\nThe smallest positive rational number \\( r \\) such that \\( \\tan r^\\circ = \\tan (87.5^\\circ) \\) is \\( r = 87.5 \\), but since we need a rational number, we use the equivalent angle within one period, which is \\( 90^\\circ - 2.5^\\circ = 87.5^\\circ \\) in the first quadrant. The smallest positive rational number is:\n\\[\nr = 87.5.\n\\]\nThus, the answer is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{87.5}.\n\\]"},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{87.5}","correct":true,"format":"boxed","parseable":true},"id":"precalculus:153"}
